#13 7.637 to use the ~name construct to specify the login directory belonging to "name",
#13 7.637 even if you don't have a shell which knows about that.  Questions where this is
#13 7.637 allowed will be marked "(~name ok)".
#13 7.637 
#13 7.637 [Type carriage return to continue]  
#13 7.640 
#13 7.640 The prompter used in this script allows you to use shell variables and
#13 7.640 backticks in your answers.  You may use $1, $2, etc...  to refer to the words
#13 7.640 in the default answer, as if the default line was a set of arguments given to a
#13 7.640 script shell.  This means you may also use $* to repeat the whole default line,
#13 7.640 so you do not have to re-type everything to add something to the default.
#13 7.640 
#13 7.640 Every time there is a substitution, you will have to confirm.  If there is an
#13 7.640 error (e.g. an unmatched backtick), the default answer will remain unchanged
#13 7.640 and you will be prompted again.
#13 7.640 
#13 7.640 If you are in a hurry, you may run 'Configure -d'.  This will bypass nearly all
#13 7.640 the questions and use the computed defaults (or the previous answers if there
